SM(526,{"n":"Romans 15-16","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Romans 15-16.mp3","d":2069.9,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest, serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.28,"Now may the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that you may abound in hope by the power of the Holy Spirit."],[29.84,"And just a note, that word believing again is the same verb as faith, and so it would be better translated, peace and faithfulness."],[37.78,"So that as you're faithful to Christ, as you're living your life of faithfulness, God would fill you with joy and peace."],[45.78,"So that you may abound in hope by the power of the Holy Spirit."],[49.94,"That sounds like a conclusion."],[52.02,"Yes, this is his second sort of benediction."],[55.78,"Remember, he said back in verse 5 Now may the God of patience and comf youort grant."],[59.46,"We're working our way, we're coming to the end here"],[60.54,"So these are his sort of parting benedictions."],[77.58,"This is that exhortation to build each other up, encourage each other."],[82.7,"Nevertheless, brethren, I have written more boldly to you on some points, as reminding you, because of the grace given to me by God."],[89.98,"So he says, you know, nevertheless, I did write this to correct you on some things."],[94.88,"To make sure that this split right doesn't happen."],[98.32,"That I might be a minister of Jesus Christ to the Gentiles, ministering the gospel of God that, the offspring of the Gentiles might be acceptable, sanctified by the Holy Spirit."],[103.76,"the Offering of Gentiles."],[113.0,"What did I say?"],[113.72,"You said offspring."],[114.76,"Oh, sorry. That the offering of the Gentiles might be acceptable, sanctified by the Holy Spirit."],[120.04,"Okay. So the word that's translated minister there, he's using an analogy of sacrifice."],[126.53,"That Jesus Christ has called on him to make an offering to him."],[132.93,"And the offering that he's making is the Gentile believers."],[138.05,"He was sent by Jesus Christ to the nations to call the Bacter Christ."],[143.09,"And now he's going to offer them to Christ."],[147.25,"Not literally, he's going to kill them all, but sacrifice them and eat them."],[148.69,"But he's offering them to God"],[156.01,"And notice what has made them an acceptable offering."],[159.85,"What has made them an acceptable offering, what has sanctified them, what has made them holy."],[164.57,"Is the Holy Spirit."],[165.69,"The Holy Spirit who has come to dwell in them in the same way the Holy Spirit came to dwell."],[170.57,"He's already used that language of living sacrifices and the Holy Spirit as filling the believer, purifying, making them clean now."],[181.51,"So they are no longer unclean as people."],[185.51,"They're no longer separated from God."],[187.85,"The Holy Spirit has made them clean."],[191.61,"This idea, including in uh St"],[191.75,"And we've seen this going all the way through Acts."],[196.85,"Peter's vision before going to Cornelius' house."],[199.41,"Do not call unclean what God has made clean."],[201.81,"Therefore I have reason to glory in Christ Jesus and the things which pertain to God."],[206.45,"For I will not dare to speak of any of those things which Christ has not accomplished through me in word and deed to make the Gentiles obedient, in mighty signs and wonders, by the power of the Spirit of God, so that from Jerusalem and roundabout to Illyricum I have fully preached the gospel of Christ."],[222.69,"He's saying there are all these uh all of these wonders, all these miracles taking place, in the lives of the Gentiles."],[230.44,"Because he's what is the relevance of this?"],[232.52,"Well, he's confirming what he just said."],[234.22,"He said the whole purpose of the Messiah."],[235.9,"The whole purpose of Israel was to produce the Messiah, the whole purpose of the Messiah was to call the nations back"],[242.92,"And he says, This is what's happening right now."],[245.48,"This is what's happening in your community."],[247.56,"He says, not just your community."],[249.64,"He says, I've traveled around."],[251.58,"From Jerusalem to Illyricum, I've traveled all around."],[254.22,"Miracles are happening."],[255.42,"Gentiles are turning."],[257.74,"Gentiles are turning to Christ."],[259.42,"The nations are turning to Christ through the Holy Spirit as he proclaims the gospel of Christ."],[265.42,"Verse 20, and so I have made up my aim to preach the gospel, not where Christ was named, lest I should build on another man's foundation."],[272.38,"That sounds weird."],[273.34,"So he says, I'm not going to places that have already heard the gospel."],[276.54,"Uh-huh. I'm not coming in afterwards."],[279.18,"Remember, he said earlier he hasn't been to Rome yet."],[280.06,"Uh-huh Someone brought the gospel to Rome, it wasn't him."],[284.98,"So he's kind of explaining why."],[287.19,"Because I've I've he's been trying, say, Paul is saying, I've been trying to go places where no one's heard the gospel yet and preach it to them."],[293.83,"Uh-huh. Not go where someone else has preached and then try and build off of that."],[298.45,"Because that's not his."],[299.57,"Not that there's something wrong with that, but that that's not his calling."],[304.05,"But as it is written, to whom he was not announced, they shall see, and those who have not heard shall understand."],[311.33,"That's Isaiah 52, verse 15."],[314.51,"He's saying this is part of the plan, too."],[318.81,"That these people who know nothing about the God of Israel."],[322.25,"Zero. Would hear the gospel proclaimed to them."],[327.65,"For this reason, I also have been much hindered from coming to you."],[330.87,"This is why I haven't come and visited you yet, the community in Rome."],[334.95,"But now no longer having a place in these parts, and having a great desire these many years to come to you, whenever I journey to Spain, I shall come to you."],[343.67,"So in addition to the Tarsus that St."],[345.67,"Paul was from, which is in what's now Turkey, there was another Tarsus or Tarshish, which was in Spain."],[351.84,"At the very southern tip of Spain, where there was a Jewish community, and that was about the furthest removed Jewish community that anybody knew of at this time."],[364.26,"And so, see, Paul is saying, you know, things aren't going so great here."],[366.82,"He said, I'm not very welcome here anymore to continue preaching"],[368.94,"We saw an acts."],[374.0,"And so I want to make this journey."],[375.6,"I want to go all the way to Spain."],[377.76,"And so when I'm on my way there, I hope to stop in Rome and visit your community there."],[383.68,"When he's under arrest and appealing to see certain things."],[386.38,"That comes to him as a good thing."],[388.38,"This is another planned trip."],[390.78,"For I hope to see you on my journey and to be helped on my way there by you."],[394.94,"At first I may enjoy your company for a while."],[397.82,"But now I am going to Jerusalem to minister to the saints."],[400.94,"So this is when he's on his way back to Jerusalem"],[405.2,"For it pleased those from Macedonia and Achaia to make a certain contribution for the poor among the saints who are in Jerusalem."],[412.16,"It pleased them indeed, and they are their debtors."],[415.04,"For if the Gentiles have been partakers of their spiritual things, their duty is also to minister to them in material things."],[421.36,"We read a little bit about this in Acts, but St."],[423.36,"Paul has been taking up a collection, essentially, because remember, the believers in Jerusalem are desperately poor."],[430.81,"They're not Roman citizens."],[433.61,"They've been persecuted on and off already in Jerusalem."],[437.61,"A couple of the apostles have been killed already."],[439.77,"Saint Stephen, obviously, has been killed already."],[442.33,"And so as he goes to these wealthier towns, and Gentiles are coming into the Christian church, many of them are more well-to-do."],[452.47,"Our Roman citizens that have more money."],[454.19,"And so he's been taking. up a collection to help them"],[458.23,"And he's saying this is appropriate."],[460.17,"Because you know, the believers of Jerusalem and Antioch have sort of sent these missionaries out to bring the gospel to all of these people."],[468.33,"And so now that there are brothers and sisters, it's good that they're now helping the poor who have done this for their sakes."],[476.97,"Therefore, when I have performed this and have sealed to them this fruit, I shall go by way of you to Spain."],[482.41,"But I know that when I come to you, I shall come in the fullness of the blessing of the gospel of Christ."],[488.09,"Now I beg you, brethren, through the Lord Jesus Christ and through the love of the Spirit, that you strive together with me in prayers to God for me."],[496.89,"Now notice the language here."],[499.33,"Through the Lord Jesus Christ and through the love of the Spirit, that you strive together with me in prayers to God for me."],[507.91,"So he's already here invoked now, the Trinity."],[512.3,"And these clearly aren't interchangeable."],[515.1,"It's pretty clear that the Lord Jesus Christ and the Spirit are not the same person."],[520.4,"And neither of them is the same person as God the Father."],[524.08,"And also, he's got the idea of praying for someone else."],[532.42,"With him. That when he prays for his mission and they pray for him, they're all praying together."],[537.94,"Uh-huh. They're all coming before God together."],[540.26,"That I may be delivered from those in Judea who do not believe or who are unfaithful."],[545.34,"And that my service for Jerusalem may be acceptable to the saints, that I may come to you with joy by the will of God, and may be refreshed together with you."],[553.9,"Now the God of peace be with you all."],[556.22,"Amen. So he says, continue praying that everything will go well in Jerusalem."],[560.3,"We know unfortunately it did not."],[563.26,"But that then he would be able to come to you."],[566.94,"Now it should be said that traditionally, and by traditionally I mean there's good reason to believe historically that Saint there was a break between the imprisonment that we read about in the book of Acts and the imprisonment that resulted in St."],[583.42,"Paul's execution. It's hard to be absolutely sure, but there's nothing in Acts that tells us that it ends during the reign of Nero."],[596.02,"In fact, there are indicators that it ends earlier than that."],[599.7,"So there are two possibilities just going by that."],[603.46,"That number one, he was imprisoned for a long period of time and then executed under Nero."],[608.82,"Or it is possible, and this is what recorded for us by the earliest church historians, that Saint Paul was released from that imprisonment, made this journey to Spain, which would be his fourth missionary journey, and then after this was arrested again, and at that point was executed under Nero."],[630.5,"So, as I say, there's good reason to believe that he did eventually this journey and either way he did get to Rome."],[631.62,"At least once"],[636.94,"Uh-huh. Yes. At least once."],[640.94,"Okay, so that is the end of chapter 15."],[643.9,"There is the formal close of the epistle as such."],[647.82,"Okay, so what's now here is this is sort of the PS the postscript to the letter."],[656.94,"I commend to you Phoebe, our sister, who is a servant of the church in Sincrea."],[661.98,"This is where they're using the New King James Version, which for various reasons reasons has chosen to render the word deaconess as servant."],[673.1,"So Phoebe was actually a uh deaconess."],[675.58,"deaconess. You know, I knew there werees, and yet it seemed odd that they were never mentioned in the Bible"],[683.22,"Yeah, they actually are."],[684.34,"Uh-huh. Uh, and when we get later into the pastoral epistles, we'll see uh St."],[689.06,"Paul directly addresses the qualifications for being a deaconess."],[693.46,"Uh-huh. A note, as we'll see then too, and I'll talk more about it then."],[697.94,"But a deaconess is not a woman who's been made a deacon."],[702.34,"Deaconess is a separate office and a separate role."],[707.94,"So uh male deacon did certain things."],[711.78,"A deaconess did certain other things."],[714.96,"She did things that the male deacon didn't do, and the male deacon did things she didn't do."],[718.96,"Uh huh. So, yeah, it's actually a slightly either in the earliest documents we have, the D Daké talks about deaconesses too, which is written around the beginning of the second century."],[730.73,"It is generally not in the form of just the word deacon but with a feminine ending."],[735.29,"Uh-huh. It usually has the word woman attached to it."],[738.33,"It's a woman deacon or a deacon woman."],[742.57,"Whereas deacon means a male deacon when it's used by itself."],[747.37,"It isn't man deacon and woman deacon."],[749.77,"It's deacon or woman deacon."],[753.17,"As a separate, as a separate office."],[757.09,"And as I said, when we get into First Timothy and Titus, we'll talk more about that."],[762.33,"And what exactly they did."],[764.45,"But this is just a mention that Phoebe, Saint Phoebe, is a is a deaconess there in the Church of Rome."],[772.73,"She's on her way there."],[773.85,"Yeah. That you may receive her in the Lord in a manner worthy of the saints and assist her in whatever business she has need of you."],[779.93,"For indeed she has been a helper of many and of myself also."],[783.63,"She's a deaconess in Sincrea."],[785.71,"And so now she's traveling to Rome, potentially on some kind of business."],[790.83,"So yeah, he's asking that they receive her there."],[794.19,"It says, Greet Priscilla and Aquilo, my fellow workers in Christ Jesus, who risked their own risked their own necks."],[800.91,"That sounds a little too up to. my life, yeah"],[805.99,"isk r Risk their life for his life, uh, to whom not only I give thanks, but also all the churches of the Gentiles likewise greet the church that is in their house."],[817.03,"So he's asking them to greet Priscilla and Aquila who are in Rome."],[820.71,"Why is this important?"],[821.83,"Well, this is one of the clues."],[824.79,"I've been saying all along that this is written to Rome after the expulsion of the Jews has ended."],[832.79,"Does anybody remember Pop Quiz where we saw Priscilla and Aquila before?"],[837.11,"No, but I remember that those are familiar names."],[840.23,"Yeah. We met them when uh St."],[842.23,"Paul first went to Corinth."],[843.91,"And we were told in Acts that uh the reason they were in Corinth is that Claudius had expelled the Jews from Rome."],[853.11,"So now they're back."],[854.31,"Uh-huh. There's a church in their house."],[861.41,"There's a gathering that takes place for the Eucharist in their house."],[865.97,"Uh 'cause they are well to do."],[867.33,"It's also interesting just as a note, and this is an oddity, that uh Priscilla is actually mentioned first and she's the wife, uh, which probably implies that she's the one who inherited the money."],[880.93,"Greet my beloved Epineetus, who is the first fruits of Achaea to Christ."],[886.93,"So he's there, he's one of the first people who uh became a Christian in Achaia."],[892.05,"Greet Mary, who labored much for us."],[894.61,"We don't know which one that is, whether it's one we've ever seen before or not."],[898.69,"You have to remember the name Mary is really the name Miriam, who was Moses' sister"],[903.61,"So as you can imagine, very common first name for Jewish, but the most common at this time in history."],[910.57,"Just as Mary was at one time, sort of John and Mary were the two sort of generic English names for people."],[917.37,"Mary was so this could be someone we've met before or not."],[923.05,"Greet Andronicus and Junior, my countrymen and my fellow prisoners who are of note among the apostles, who also were in Christ before me."],[931.45,"Now notice it says, My fellow prisoners."],[934.01,"A minute ago, he was on his way to Jerusalem."],[937.37,"So there's a couple possibilities here."],[939.69,"One is that this postscript gets tacked on afterwards."],[944.01,"After Saint Paul is arrested"],[946.13,"Uh huh. Meaning the letter didn't actually get sent."],[952.29,"Now remember, we're not dropping it in a mailbox."],[955.25,"So someone had to carry it."],[957.27,"After St. Paul was done editing it, someone had to carry it to Rome, and whoever it was was not dispatched until after St."],[963.99,"Paul's arrest. So that's very possible."],[967.05,"Because he wasn't in Jerusalem very long before he got arrested."],[973.85,"Well, he got he he got in trouble a number of times."],[977.97,"so Well, that's true too."],[980.41,"But the other times it doesn't it doesn't seem like he would have had time to write a letter."],[985.45,"Yeah Um well if he's a prisoner when he's sending this."],[990.93,"There isn't a sort of an opportune time in the book of Acts."],[993.49,"Like when he was in Philippi, they were there overnight."],[996.05,"Yeah. You know."],[997.49,"I just figured that these were people I I mean I read it as these were people that had been in jail with him at the first time."],[1006.13,"That's also possible."],[1008.29,"That's also possible."],[1009.41,"It's uh it's also but like I said that he's using it metaphorically."],[1013.01,"Uh that they're he's using it in terms of prisoner in terms of a slave as in their servants of Christ is also possible."],[1020.93,"But again, like I said, it's also possible that this postscript is added, you know."],[1025.45,"You know, uh, after he, you know, he wrote the letter, he arrives in Jerusalem, he's thrown in prison, he dispatches someone to bring the letter in and, so now he's a prisoner."],[1033.25,"uh And notice he says that they are of note among the apostles, meaning in Jerusalem, the Church of Jerusalem, and were in Christ before me, meaning they've been Christians longer than St."],[1046.57,"Paul has. They may have been 70 or something."],[1049.45,"Yeah, and the my countrymen means these are Jewish, these are part of that original group."],[1054.41,"Uh-huh. Maybe from Pentecost, maybe even from previous to that."],[1059.13,"Greet Amplius, my beloved in the Lord, greet Urbanus, our fellow worker in Christ, and Stachis, my beloved."],[1066.01,"Greet Apelles, approved in Christ."],[1068.17,"Greet those who are of the household of Aristobulus."],[1070.89,"Greet Herodian, my countrymen, greet those who are of the household of Narcissus who are in the Lord."],[1076.49,"Um notice as St."],[1080.37,"Paul is running through all these people he knows."],[1082.77,"Notice the mix and the fact that he's not making a distinction."],[1087.09,"He isn't greet all these Jewish people, now greet all these Gentile people."],[1091.43,"They're all mixed together."],[1092.31,"And some of these, like Narcissus, who's named after a Greek uh Greek pagan Greek god."],[1100.31,"Uh some of these are very obviously very obviously pagan converts."],[1106.37,"Or Herodians Some of these are unclear."],[1109.09,"Well, yeah, he says Herodian, my countrymen."],[1110.85,"Uh-huh. Uh some of them are very clearly Jewish, and some of them it's ambiguous."],[1116.05,"Greet Trifena and Triphosa, who have labored in the Lord, greet the beloved Persis, who labored much in in the the L Lordord, greet Rufus, chosen, and his mother and mine."],[1121.81,"Uh that's not saying that it's his brother"],[1129.43,"That's saying that his mother greet him and his mother, and his mother has been like a mother to St."],[1135.67,"Paul. Greet Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermes, Patrobus, Hermes, another pagan Greek god, and the brethren who are with them, greet Philologus and Julia, and Araeus and his sister, and Olympus and all the saints who are with them."],[1151.53,"Greet one another with a holy kiss, the churches of Christ greet you."],[1156.25,"Okay So notice, even though he hasn't been there, how many people St."],[1160.65,"Paul knows who are in the church in Rome."],[1162.89,"So if you wonder, well, how can he know what's going on there there? if he's never been"],[1167.97,"Uh-huh. Well, he knows an awful lot of people who are there."],[1172.21,"Uh, and including like Priscilla and Aquila, probably some of these others who are labeled as his countrymen, who are Jewish, who have been able to recently return to Rome, and so that would be how he is aware of the the situation."],[1189.57,"Now I urge you, brethren, note those who cause divisions and offenses, contrary to the doctrine which you learned, and avoid them."],[1197.34,"So this is this is hi another post."],[1200.22,"This is P uh PPS or PSS."],[1203.56,"The first PS."],[1204.74,"This is really what he's been talking about."],[1206.06,"Because he's been talking about unity."],[1207.3,"This is the flip side of that."],[1208.98,"If there are are people in your community who are going around and causing division and offenses, who stirring up against this."],[1209.08,"If there are, note those."],[1217.67,"Who are teaching against what I've just said in this letter."],[1223.27,"Avoid them. Avoid them."],[1226.41,"For those who are such do not serve our Lord Jesus Christ, but their own belly."],[1230.89,"And by smooth words and flattering speech deceive the hearts of the simple."],[1235.29,"Okay? So they're out for themselves."],[1238.55,"The uh the serving their own belly means they're trying to enrich themselves and serve themselves and draw off a following for themselves rather than trying to help others to follow Christ."],[1251.03,"For your obedience has become known to all, therefore I am glad on your behalf."],[1255.47,"But I want you to be wise in what is good and simple concerning evil."],[1259.55,"He says, I want you to be wise in what is good, meaning I want you to know everything, learn everything that is good."],[1266.19,"I want you to be simple in terms of what is evil."],[1268.83,"I want you to be dumb in terms of what is evil."],[1271.71,"I want you to know what good is and not know what evil is."],[1275.21,"I want you to not know anything about it."],[1278.41,"And the God of peace will crush Satan under your feet shortly."],[1282.41,"What's he referencing there?"],[1284.49,"Crushing Satan under your feet."],[1286.17,"Final judgment That goes back to Genesis 3."],[1288.81,"Yeah. Remember? Seat of the woman."],[1292.07,"He will strike his heel, but he will crush his."],[1294.75,"He will crush his head."],[1295.83,"Uh-huh So remember, remember what we were just saying."],[1298.96,"All this plan from the very beginning."],[1301.58,"The first time the gospel is announced in Genesis 3."],[1305.12,"About the seed of the woman, about Christ."],[1307.12,"The whole purpose of this is coming to fruition in the community in Rome."],[1313.92,"This is happening in and among you."],[1317.36,"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you, Amen."],[1320.96,"And then St."],[1321.76,"Paul remembers he forgot a few more people."],[1324.8,"And he's prone to doing this."],[1326.12,"You remember we read we read it a few weeks ago in this epistle where he says, Well, I'm glad I didn't baptize anyone there."],[1332.0,"Except so and so and so and so."],[1334.24,"Well, in so and so's household and so and so."],[1336.72,"Yeah. Well, in so and so."],[1337.86,"so. But we've got we've got a few more people"],[1339.02,"And if I baptize anybody else, I don't remember."],[1346.14,"Timothy, my fellow worker, and Lucius, Jason, and Sosapater, my countrymen, greet you."],[1352.07,"So these are people who are with him, uh huh."],[1353.93,"Who want to say hi to you."],[1356.49,"I, Tertius, who wrote this epistle, greet you in the Lord."],[1359.61,"I know I referenced this in the first one."],[1361.53,"This is this is the trick Bible question, uh huh."],[1364.19,"Who wrote Saint Paul's epistle to the Romans?"],[1367.07,"And everybody says St."],[1367.95,"Paul, and you take him here and you say, No, Tertius."],[1371.71,"Uh-hhu. What does this mean?"],[1373.09,"Tertius is the what was called in Greek in Emanuensis."],[1376.69,"He's the scribe who's actually writing."],[1378.93,"We talked about that how St."],[1381.25,"Paul didn't actually sit down and write any of these letters longhand."],[1385.93,"Couldn't he write?"],[1387.61,"Yes. He could, because we know in a few places he says, see with what big letters I'm writing to you."],[1393.61,"In two different places in the letters in my own hand."],[1397.51,"So there were a couple places where to make a point."],[1399.67,"He said, I'm writing this myself."],[1402.15,"Uh-huh. To make to make a point."],[1404.76,"But that was not the normal process for formal letter writing."],[1408.44,"The way that happened was he would dictate to, in this case, Tertius."],[1413.18,"Tertius would write it down, polish up the grammar, and everything, make it not make it look nice."],[1418.58,"And then he would give it back to Saint Paul, who would go over it and make any corrections he wanted to make."],[1425.24,"No. I meant da-da-da, or phrase it this way instead, or you know, I didn't want you to correct my grammar"],[1431.84,"That's how I want it."],[1432.65,"Whatever it was."],[1433.93,"And then uh Tertius would have also been the one who would have brought the letter to Rome and read it to them publicly in the community, and then he would have been expected to be prepared to answer any questions they had about it, um, or anything they didn't understand."],[1454.17,"Uh now the name Tertius means third."],[1457.05,"This was very common in Roman names."],[1459.13,"Romans had four names."],[1461.69,"Uh the first name was their given name."],[1464.55,"And then it was the name of their uh father, their grandfather, and then an ancestor."],[1469.59,"An important ancestor"],[1476.99,"And because of this, most Roman fathers considered themselves more important than their sons."],[1487.23,"And the grandfather was more important than the father."],[1489.57,"And the ancestor was more important than all of them."],[1491.97,"But because of this sort of hierarchical thing, a lot of people's given names, a lot of fathers would give their sons names like Primus, Secundus, Tertius, Quadratus, meaning first, second, third, fourth."],[1509.17,"And then their father's name, their grandfather's n.ame"],[1512.63,"Yeah, eighth in the case book."],[1514.15,"But that was his that was his given name"],[1514.53,"Which is why he didn't go by Octavian."],[1520.21,"So Tertius was the third son of his father."],[1525.58,"And that's why his name is Tertius."],[1527.66,"Um this custom was revived in English public schools, where brothers uh went through the school."],[1537.5,"The oldest one was Primus, and the next one was Secundus."],[1542.6,"And so and and it's so it's not totally dissimilar from the common practice now of a father giving his son the exact same name."],[1554.52,"And then him being junior, and then him giving his son the exact same name, so he's the third."],[1558.28,"Yeah So this is their version of that."],[1567.2,"Gaius, my host, and the host of the whole church greet you, greets you."],[1572.32,"Erastus, the treasurer of the city, greets you, and Cortus."],[1575.92,"There's another one."],[1578.56,"A brother. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all."],[1582.08,"Amen. And so now we have the final, the final, final benediction."],[1586.64,"I know it seems like this is ending more than the return of the king."],[1589.52,"Yeah. But but this is this is typical structure for a formal letter."],[1596.64,"It says, Now to him who is able to establish you according to my gospel in the preaching of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery kept secret since the world began, but now made manifest, and by the prophetic scriptures made known to all nations, according to the commandment of the everlasting God, for obedience to the faith, to God alone wise be glory through Jesus Christ forever."],[1619.96,"Amen. He's now summarized a lot of what he's just said here in this final benediction."],[1639.4,"To him, and he's going to say in verse 27, to God."],[1643.56,"So he's talking about God the Father, who is able to establish you."],[1648.88,"That establish is related to that word, that idea of building up."],[1653.14,"He's able to establish you according to my gospel and the preaching of Jesus Christ."],[1658.44,"Which is what he's proclaimed to him."],[1659.96,"He's proclaimed to them Jesus Christ, his incarnation, his life, his death, his resurrection, his ascension into heaven and enthronement, and then he's going to return to judge the living and the dead."],[1674.12,"And so that's what that's how they're going to be established."],[1677.8,"They're going to be established in Christ through what Christ has done."],[1681.24,"According to the revelation of the mystery kept secret since the world began."],[1685.8,"Now that's according to is the same thing he just said."],[1688.6,"So he's paralleling those two things."],[1691.08,"So what Christ has done, the gospel that's been proclaimed to them, is the mystery, which has had been kept secret since the world began."],[1703.38,"Notice, now he's going back even farther."],[1707.38,"He's kept going back and back and back."],[1709.15,"We went back to Deuteronomy 32."],[1710.75,"He said that's one of the oldest things in the Bible."],[1713.15,"A few verses ago, he went back to Genesis 3."],[1718.59,"The first gospel."],[1720.19,"Now we're back to before the world began, before the beginning, before the creation."],[1727.69,"So Christ, at all of those things we just said, all those things which Christ did, that's not only the reason why God brought Israel into existence."],[1739.53,"That's not only what God had planned in response to humanity being expelled from paradise."],[1746.81,"This is why God created the world."],[1749.61,"That's pretty basic."],[1751.21,"Was for the purpose of Jesus Christ."],[1754.26,"And it was kept a secret."],[1755.78,"Why was it kept a secret?"],[1762.32,"Why was it kept a secret?"],[1763.68,"Well, people couldn't wouldn't have understood it."],[1765.92,"Well, one of the speeches in Acts tells us that Paul says, if they had known, they would not have crucified."],[1772.44,"If they had known the powers of the powers of this age, if they had known, would not have crucified the Lord of glory."],[1780.08,"It's talking about who's behind the Romans"],[1781.06,"Now the powers of this age is not talking about the Romans."],[1783.62,"No. We talk about that's Satan in this Indian."],[1789.46,"It's referenced here."],[1790.9,"This is referenced in one of our hymns."],[1794.82,"The mystery which was hidden from everlasting and was unknown by the angels."],[1801.95,"Was what? Made manifest through the Theotokos through Christ's birth to those who dwell upon earth."],[1810.85,"So this is that idea."],[1812.29,"They didn't know."],[1814.63,"They didn't know."],[1816.39,"And he says Father."],[1820.03,"Yeah About the humans."],[1820.09,"About the humans."],[1821.21,"Yeah. And so, so that's why it's hidden."],[1829.36,"That's why it's hidden all this time."],[1831.6,"But now, that gospel, the gospel, which is the recounting of that, of the victory that Christ has won over those dark powers."],[1840.84,"Has now been made manifest, has now been made known by the prophetic scriptures made known the prophetic writing, the prophetic things which were made known to all nations."],[1852.82,"To all nations."],[1854.98,"Well, not just bringing the nations in, but he's referring to the prophetic scriptures."],[1859.7,"Uh-huh. Which is what?"],[1862.24,"That whole tradition of Is Israelra.el has been made known through this whole tradition in"],[1869.16,"Through the whole history of Israel, which is what's recounted in the prophets."],[1873.4,"That's why he says the prophetic writings in particular."],[1876.37,"The whole history of Israel, through the whole history of Israel, has been made known to all the nations."],[1883.19,"So he's connected those two again."],[1886.89,"And the gospel is what brings those two things together."],[1889.93,"Christ is the fulfillment of the scriptures and the promises made to the fathers, and he is the hope and the welcoming of the return of the of the nations."],[1903.69,"According to the commandment of the everlasting God for obedience to the faith."],[1908.25,"the faith. I would translate that as for obedience of faithfulness, but or forful obedience"],[1914.85,"But what's he just drawn together there?"],[1919.97,"We're going back to chapter three in particular, where he talked about faithfulness or faith as it's usually translated, and works of the law."],[1933.55,"Works of the law, the commandments."],[1935.47,"According to the commandment of the everlasting God for faithful obedience."],[1941.81,"The commandments of the law, the commandments were given to Israel."],[1946.61,"To Israel, so that the church could be everyone could be faithful and obedient."],[1952.77,"To God Drawing those two together again."],[1956.25,"And then he goes back to God, to him."],[1960.06,"Alone wise be glory."],[1961.9,"Through Jesus Christ forever."],[1964.22,"Amen. So this is the end of St."],[1968.7,"Paul's Epistle to the Romans."],[1971.42,"Next time we will get started on 1 Corinthians."],[1976.78,"In the introduction, we'll talk a little bit about Corinth, which is an interesting city."],[1984.62,"There's going to be a lot of serious problems at the church in Corinth."],[1991.82,"But this is this is something from which all modern Christians should take heart."],[1996.78,"all And I'll end with this that Christian churches, because in some churches, not ours, of course, but in some churches, there are a lot of problems."],[2010.74,"Hard to believe."],[2017.06,"But in other churches, in other parishes, in other places, there are problems."],[2024.9,"And let me assure you, they pale in comparison to the problems that were going on in Corinth in the first century, uh as we will see."],[2036.46,"Uh, some of them be truly horrific."],[2038.58,"Well, that's a good teaser."],[2040.02,"Yeah. So, but we'll begin talking about that next time."],[2044.7,"So, thank you, everybody."],[2046.06,"Thank you. Listen next time as Father Stephen De Young continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2054.78,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecouncil at ancientfaith.com."],[2060.14,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.28,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 15:13 - God of hope","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"May the <b>God of hope</b> fill you with all <b>joy and peace in believing</b>, that you may abound in hope by the power of the <b>Holy Spirit</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Believing\" = same verb as <b>faith</b> → better: <b>peace and faithfulness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">as you're faithful to Christ, living faithfulness, God fills you with joy and peace</li><li class=\"d0\">Sounds like a conclusion - his <b>second benediction</b> (first: v. 5, \"God of patience and comfort\")</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>parting benedictions</b> - the exhortation to <b>build each other up</b></li></ul>"},{"t":82.7,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 15:14-16 - Minister of Christ to the Gentiles","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Nevertheless, I have written <b>more boldly</b> on some points\" - did write to <b>correct</b> you, so the <b>split doesn't happen</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul = \"minister of Jesus Christ to the Gentiles\"; the <b>offering of the Gentiles</b> acceptable, <b>sanctified by the Holy Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"minister\" = <b>sacrifice analogy</b> - Christ called him to make an <b>offering</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the offering = <b>Gentile believers</b> - he calls them, now <b>offers them to God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not literally - \"sacrifice them and eat them\" (joke)</li><li class=\"d0\">What makes them acceptable: the <b>Holy Spirit</b> dwelling in them</li><li class=\"d1\">already used <b>living sacrifices</b> language (ch. 12)</li><li class=\"d1\">no longer <b>unclean</b>, no longer <b>separated from God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">through Acts: <b>Peter's vision</b> before Cornelius - \"<b>do not call unclean what God has made clean</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":201.81,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 15:17-19 - Fully preached from Jerusalem to Illyricum","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"I have reason to glory in Christ Jesus\" - speaks only of what <b>Christ accomplished through him</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>signs and wonders</b>, by the power of the Spirit; \"from <b>Jerusalem to Illyricum</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Relevance: <b>confirms what he just said</b></li><li class=\"d1\">purpose of <b>Israel</b> = produce the <b>Messiah</b>; purpose of Messiah = <b>call the nations back</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"this is what's happening <b>right now</b>\" - in your community, and everywhere he's traveled</li><li class=\"d1\">miracles, <b>Gentiles turning to Christ</b> through the Spirit</li></ul>"},{"t":265.42,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 15:20-21 - Not building on another's foundation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Preach the gospel <b>not where Christ was named</b>, lest I build on another man's foundation\"</li><li class=\"d1\">only goes where no one has heard; not coming in afterwards</li><li class=\"d1\">hasn't been to Rome - <b>someone else brought the gospel there</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"not that there's something wrong with that\" - <b>not his calling</b></li><li class=\"d0\">v. 21: \"To whom he was not announced they shall see\" - <b>Isaiah 52:15</b></li><li class=\"d1\">part of the plan: people who know <b>zero</b> about the God of Israel hear the gospel</li></ul>"},{"t":327.65,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 15:22-24 - Plans to visit Rome via Spain","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Why he hasn't come to Rome: \"much hindered\"; no more place in these parts; long desire</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Whenever I journey to <b>Spain</b>\" - another <b>Tarsus / Tarshish</b> at the <b>southern tip of Spain</b></li><li class=\"d1\">had a <b>Jewish community</b>, furthest-removed one anyone knew of</li><li class=\"d0\">Things not going great: \"<b>not very welcome</b> here to continue preaching\" (Acts)</li><li class=\"d0\">Hope: stop in Rome on the way, be <b>helped on my way</b> by you; enjoy your company a while</li><li class=\"d1\">later under arrest, appealing to Caesar - <b>another planned trip</b> coming good</li></ul>"},{"t":397.82,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 15:25-29 - Collection for the saints in Jerusalem","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Now I am going to <b>Jerusalem</b> to minister to the saints\" - on his way back</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Macedonia and Achaia</b> contribution for the <b>poor</b> saints in Jerusalem</li><li class=\"d1\">Jerusalem believers <b>desperately poor</b>, not Roman citizens, <b>persecuted</b> on and off</li><li class=\"d1\">apostles killed already - <b>St. Stephen</b></li><li class=\"d1\">wealthier Gentile towns, many <b>well-to-do Roman citizens</b> → he takes up a <b>collection</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"They are their <b>debtors</b>\" - Gentiles partook of <b>spiritual things</b>, duty to minister <b>material things</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Jerusalem and <b>Antioch</b> sent the missionaries out</li><li class=\"d0\">Then \"I shall go by way of you to Spain\" - \"in the <b>fullness of the blessing</b> of the gospel of Christ\"</li></ul>"},{"t":488.09,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 15:30-33 - Strive together in prayer","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Through the <b>Lord Jesus Christ</b> and the <b>love of the Spirit</b>\" - strive with me in prayers to God</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Trinity</b> already invoked - Christ and Spirit <b>not interchangeable</b>, neither is the Father</li><li class=\"d1\">praying for each other: \"all <b>coming before God together</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Prayer: delivered from <b>unbelieving/unfaithful in Judea</b>; service <b>acceptable to the saints</b>; come to you with <b>joy</b>, refreshed</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Now the <b>God of peace</b> be with you all. Amen\" - third benediction</li><li class=\"d1\">continue praying it goes well in Jerusalem - \"we know unfortunately it did not\"</li></ul>"},{"t":566.94,"lv":3,"h":"Did Paul get to Spain?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Good reason to think a <b>break between</b> the Acts imprisonment and the one ending in <b>execution</b></li><li class=\"d1\">nothing in Acts says it ends under <b>Nero</b>; indicators it ends <b>earlier</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Two possibilities</li><li class=\"d1\">imprisoned a long time, then executed under Nero</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>released</b>, made the <b>Spain journey</b> (his <b>fourth missionary journey</b>), arrested again, executed under Nero - <b>earliest church historians</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Either way he got to <b>Rome</b> at least once</li><li class=\"d0\">End of chapter 15 = formal close; ch. 16 = the <b>PS</b></li></ul>"},{"t":656.94,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 16:1-2 - Phoebe the deaconess","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"I commend to you <b>Phoebe</b>, our sister, <b>servant of the church in Cenchrea</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">NKJV renders <b>deaconess</b> as \"servant\" - she was a <b>deaconess</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: why never mentioned in the Bible? - they are</li><li class=\"d1\">more in the <b>pastoral epistles</b>: qualifications for deaconess</li><li class=\"d0\">Deaconess ≠ woman made a <b>deacon</b> - <b>separate office, separate role</b></li><li class=\"d1\">male deacon did some things, she did others the deacon didn't</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Didache</b> (~start of 2nd c.) mentions deaconesses too</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>\"woman deacon\"</b> or \"deacon woman\" - plain \"deacon\" = male; not \"man deacon / woman deacon\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Phoebe traveling to Rome on <b>business</b> - \"receive her in the Lord worthily\", assist her</li><li class=\"d1\">\"a <b>helper of many</b> and of myself also\"</li></ul>"},{"t":794.19,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 16:3-5 - Priscilla and Aquila","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Greet <b>Priscilla and Aquila</b>, my fellow workers... who <b>risked their own necks</b> for my life\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Clue: Romans written <b>after the expulsion of the Jews ended</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Pop quiz: met them when Paul first went to <b>Corinth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Acts: there because <b>Claudius expelled the Jews</b> from Rome → <b>now back</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"The <b>church in their house</b>\" - <b>Eucharist</b> gathering in their home; they're <b>well to do</b></li><li class=\"d1\">oddity: <b>Priscilla mentioned first</b>, the wife → probably <b>she inherited the money</b></li></ul>"},{"t":880.93,"lv":3,"h":"Romans 16:5-7 - Epaenetus, Mary, Andronicus and Junia","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Epaenetus</b> - <b>first fruits of Achaia</b> to Christ</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Mary</b> - labored much; <b>Miriam</b>, Moses' sister; most common Jewish name then, like \"<b>John and Mary</b>\" in English - can't tell if we've met her</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Andronicus and Junia(s)</b> - \"my countrymen and <b>fellow prisoners</b>, <b>of note among the apostles</b>, in Christ <b>before me</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"fellow prisoners\" - but he was just heading to Jerusalem</li><li class=\"d0\">Options: <b>postscript tacked on after his arrest</b> - letter not yet dispatched</li><li class=\"d1\">no mailbox - someone had to <b>carry it</b>; he wasn't in Jerusalem long before arrest</li><li class=\"d1\">other times (Philippi overnight) <b>no time to write</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Or earlier jail time with him; or <b>\"prisoner\" metaphorical</b> = servants of Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Of note among the apostles\" = Church of <b>Jerusalem</b>; Christians <b>longer than Paul</b> - maybe the <b>70</b>, from <b>Pentecost</b> or before; countrymen = Jewish</li></ul>"},{"t":1059.13,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 16:8-16 - The greetings: Jews and Gentiles mixed","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Ampliatus, Urbanus, Stachys, Apelles, household of <b>Aristobulus</b>, <b>Herodion</b>, household of <b>Narcissus</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Tryphena, Tryphosa, Persis; <b>Rufus</b> \"and his mother and mine\"</li><li class=\"d1\">mother <b>like a mother</b> to Paul - not his brother</li><li class=\"d0\">Asyncritus, Phlegon, <b>Hermes</b>, Patrobas, Philologus, Julia, Nereus and sister, Olympas</li><li class=\"d0\">Notice the <b>mix</b> - he doesn't separate Jews and Gentiles</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Narcissus</b>, <b>Hermes</b> - named after <b>pagan Greek</b> figures → pagan converts</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Herodion</b> \"my countrymen\" - clearly Jewish; some ambiguous</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Greet one another with a <b>holy kiss</b>; the churches of Christ greet you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul knows <b>many people</b> in Rome though never there</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Priscilla and Aquila</b>, Jewish returnees → how he knows the situation</li></ul>"},{"t":1189.57,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 16:17-20 - Note those who cause divisions","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Note</b> those who cause <b>divisions and offenses</b>, contrary to the doctrine you learned, and <b>avoid them</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>flip side of unity</b> - another PS</li><li class=\"d1\">those teaching <b>against what I've written in this letter</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Serve not Christ but <b>their own belly</b>\" - smooth words, flattery deceive the <b>simple</b></li><li class=\"d1\">enrich themselves, <b>draw a following</b> for themselves instead of helping others follow Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Wise in what is good, simple concerning evil</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">know everything good; \"<b>dumb</b> in terms of evil\" - not know anything about it</li><li class=\"d0\">\"God of peace will <b>crush Satan under your feet</b> shortly\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Genesis 3</b>: seed of the woman strikes his heel, <b>crushes his head</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the first announcement of the gospel → purpose <b>coming to fruition in the community in Rome</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1320.96,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 16:21-24 - Greetings from Paul's companions","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you\" - then Paul remembers a few more people</li><li class=\"d1\">prone to this - cf. <b>1 Corinthians</b> \"glad I baptized none except...\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Timothy, Lucius, Jason, Sosipater</b> greet you</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"I, Tertius, who wrote this epistle\"</b> - trick question: who wrote Romans?</li><li class=\"d1\">Tertius = <b>amanuensis</b>, the scribe who actually wrote</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul could write: \"see what <b>large letters</b>\" - writes himself in <b>two places</b> to make a point</li><li class=\"d1\">normal process: <b>dictate</b> → Tertius writes, <b>polishes grammar</b> → Paul reviews and corrects (\"I meant this, phrase it this way\")</li><li class=\"d1\">Tertius probably <b>carried the letter to Rome</b>, read it <b>publicly</b>, and <b>answered questions</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Gaius</b>, host of the whole church; <b>Erastus</b>, city <b>treasurer</b>; <b>Quartus</b>, a brother</li></ul>"},{"t":1454.17,"lv":3,"h":"Roman names: Tertius = \"third\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Romans had <b>four names</b>: given name, father's, grandfather's, an <b>important ancestor</b>'s</li><li class=\"d1\">fathers saw themselves as more important than sons, grandfathers more, ancestor most</li><li class=\"d0\">So given names like <b>Primus, Secundus, Tertius, Quartus</b> = first, second, third, fourth</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Octavian</b> - didn't go by Octavius (eighth)</li><li class=\"d1\">Tertius = <b>third son</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Revived in <b>English public schools</b> - brothers Primus, Secundus</li><li class=\"d1\">not unlike son named after father: <b>Junior</b>, then <b>the third</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1582.08,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 16:25-27 - Final benediction: God able to establish you","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Final, final benediction\" - <b>typical formal letter structure</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Now to him who is able to <b>establish</b> you according to my gospel and the preaching of Jesus Christ...\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>summarizes</b> much of the letter</li><li class=\"d1\">\"him\" (v. 27: \"to God\") = <b>God the Father</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>establish</b> = related to <b>building up</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"My gospel and the preaching of Jesus Christ\" - what he's proclaimed</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>incarnation, life, death, resurrection, ascension, enthronement</b>, return to judge the living and the dead</li><li class=\"d1\">established <b>in Christ through what Christ has done</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1681.24,"lv":3,"h":"\"The mystery kept secret since the world began\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"According to\" paralleled: gospel proclaimed = the <b>mystery kept secret since the world began</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Going back and back: <b>Deut. 32</b> (oldest) → <b>Genesis 3</b> (first gospel) → <b>before creation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not only why God brought <b>Israel</b> into being, or his response to the <b>expulsion from paradise</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"This is <b>why God created the world</b>\" - <b>for the purpose of Jesus Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why secret? If they'd known they <b>would not have crucified the Lord of glory</b> (1 Cor. 2)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>powers of this age</b> = <b>not the Romans</b> - <b>Satan</b> and the dark powers</li><li class=\"d1\">hymn: the mystery \"<b>hidden from everlasting and unknown by the angels</b>... made manifest through the <b>Theotokos</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Now made manifest: the gospel = <b>victory Christ won over the dark powers</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1840.84,"lv":3,"h":"\"Made known to all nations\" by the prophetic scriptures","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"By the <b>prophetic scriptures</b> made known to all nations\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not just bringing nations in - the <b>whole history of Israel</b>, as told in the prophets, made known to them</li><li class=\"d0\">The gospel brings the two together</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ = <b>fulfillment of scriptures and promises to the fathers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">and the <b>hope and welcoming back of the nations</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Obedience to the faith</b>\" - better <b>obedience of faithfulness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">back to <b>ch. 3</b>: faithfulness and <b>works of the law</b></li><li class=\"d1\">commandments given to Israel so that <b>everyone</b> could be faithful and obedient to God - the two drawn together</li><li class=\"d0\">\"To God alone wise be <b>glory through Jesus Christ forever</b>. Amen\" - <b>end of Romans</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1971.42,"lv":2,"h":"Next: 1 Corinthians","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Next time: begin <b>1 Corinthians</b>, intro on <b>Corinth</b>, \"an interesting city\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Many <b>serious problems</b> at the Corinthian church - take heart</li><li class=\"d1\">problems in other parishes today \"<b>pale in comparison</b>\" to first-century Corinth</li><li class=\"d1\">some \"truly <b>horrific</b>\"</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next time: <b>1 Corinthians</b> - intro and Corinth"});
